# Shipping stack

- **Current game:** `src/` (Lite / WebGPU). Local: `src/index.html`. Ship: `npm run package` in `src/` → `DEPLOY/` (S3/CloudFront).
- **Deprecated:** root `index.html`, `game/`, `vendor/babylon9*`. Babylon 9 JS stack. Do not add features here unless the user explicitly asks to touch the legacy build.
- `src/forge/game/` is the forge copy, not the deprecated root `game/` tree.

If a task is "the game" or "what ships", work in `src/`.

## Distribution

Ship only through the documented upload. Web: `npm run package` in `src/`, then upload `DEPLOY/` per `DEVGUIDE`. Steam: `npm run upload:steam` in `steam-build`, then the user sets the build live.

Never build a local-only package and treat it as shipped. Never edit the Steam library install (`steamapps/common/Aether.Garden`, including `aether.url`, `package.nw`, or anything beside the exe). A local build or an install edit happens only after the user confirms that, more than once, in the same request.
